  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe [`scrollRestoration`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#dom-history-scroll-restoration) getter and setter steps both refer to \"this's node navigable\", but as far as I can tell `History` does not have one.\n\nFurther down in [delta traverse](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#dom-history-scroll-restoration) the relevant global object's associated document's node navigable is used. I'm guessing that should be what `scrollRestoration` refers to as well.\n\nPinging @domenic as #11204 is what led me to notice this.",
